  "engineering_findings": [
    "Native layout matters independently of dtype. R209 ordinary F16 NHWC/pass0 was 23.656% slower than its own F32 control. This trial changes both the blocked layout and pass-through path; it is not the same intervention.",
    "Native packing still costs 44.160 ms versus 14.776 ms for the same-run F32 route, but three-owner dispatch/drain decreases from 266.201 ms to 177.889 ms. These measured phases include opaque SDK IO; no vendor-internal cause is established.",
    "Per-owner inputs_set means decrease from 64.565/103.068/102.639 ms to 2.109/2.656/2.808 ms. Summed concurrent SDK run time increases from 420.387 ms to 444.922 ms, so the complete-call gain is not evidence that attention kernel execution became faster.",
    "All 16 heads, 2082 query rows/full 2082 keys and 64 original value components remain. Completion is only FLOAT32 axis2 concatenation; no sentinel, denominator, centering, fitted correction or attention-mask change."
  ],
  "decision": "Retain the exact-model native-input representation and bounded component finding for further integration work. Do not change the complete-model default or accept original-FP32 quality from these failed tensor gates.",
